[[File:Assorted_meat_pepper_soup_at_Lagos_Island.jpg|thumb|A bowl of peppersoup with different meats]]
'''Peppersoup''' (or pepper soup) is a [[soup]] eaten by [[Cameroonians]] and [[Nigerians]]. This soup is made using various meats or fish, [[chili pepper|chili peppers]], salt, [[Ocimum gratissimum|scent leaves]] and [[calabash nutmeg]] as its primary ingredients. It is a [[Pungency|spicy]] soup that has a light, watery texture. Despite its name, the soup is not necessarily defined by a pepper-forward [[Taste|flavor]] profile; the flavors are more complex, with nutty, bitter, woodsy, and floral notes, as well as warmth.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Nigerian Pepper Soup |url=https://www.seriouseats.com/nigerian-pepper-soup-5323040 |access-date=2022-07-23 |website=Serious Eats |language=en}}</ref> It is considered a [[delicacy]] by some people in [[West Africa|Western Africa]], and some West Africans believe that the soup has some basic medicinal qualities.
